WHATNOW

What tam-pane is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-26, with W33


STATE

  Version 0.2.8 on branch dev (W33): adds configuration and IPC primitives
  for Tamlinux 0.7.0 Milestone 6 (Port bosgame's controls): `tp.monitor`
  geometry/mode/scale/transform rules with live reload; XKB (`kb_layout`,
  `kb_variant`, `kb_model`, `kb_options`, `kb_rules`, `numlock_by_default`)
  and pointer (`natural_scroll`, `scroll_factor`) config; `tp.home`,
  `tp.config_dir`, and `tp.include(path[, optional])`; `code:<N>` keycodes,
  `{ release = true }` binds, `tp.mouse_bind`/`tp.mouse_unbind`,
  `tp.dsp.focus("left"|"right"|"up"|"down")`, `tp.dsp.send_key`,
  `tp.dsp.capture`, `tp.dsp.mouse_move`, `tp.dsp.mouse_resize`; IPC
  `id`/`pid` on windows, `phys_w`/`phys_h`/`refresh`/`transform` on
  monitors, and `dispatch send_key|capture|monitor scale|focus <dir>`.

  Prior version 0.2.7 (W32, 418bd62): shell IPC queries, DPMS/app/keyboard
  dispatches, and events for Milestone 5.

  Prior accepted baseline: 0.2.6 (accepted by Fred on 2026-11-23, W31),
  including opt-in XWayland support behind `XWAYLAND=1` (default
  `XWAYLAND=0` produces a zero-xcb build with `-DTP_XWAYLAND=0`),
  `sandbox/demo-x11.c`, and one-handed chord composer (`7ca46a8`).

  Prior accepted baseline: 0.2.5 (1eec348, accepted 2026-11-23, W30).
  Review R1 (reviews/R1-code-review-0.1.4.md) findings 1-10, 12-16, and
  finding 17's binding gate and SIGHUP point are done; finding 11 waits
  for P4, and finding 17's remaining smaller points land alongside the P4
  versions that need them.

  Automated checks pass for both XWAYLAND=0 (28 tag, 143 dwindle, 102
  layouts, 537 Lua, 111 IPC, 5 smoke, 743 headless input, zero libxcb
  NEEDED) and XWAYLAND=1 (764 headless input including real Xwayland +
